OL,3,GNEWSAPumpkin patch saved by lucky
OL,4,Adecision last year
OL,5,
OL,6,FPumpkins are an iconic part of
OL,7,FHalloween for many, but the summer's
OL,8,Fextreme heat has had an impact on this
OL,9,Fyear's crop.
OL,11,FFor some farms in the south of England,
OL,12,Fthe droughts mean their pick your own
OL,13,Fpatches will not be able to open their
OL,14,Fgates this season, or the harvests have
OL,15,Fbeen reduced.
OL,17,FFortunately for Halloween fans in the
OL,18,FNorth East, pumpkins are faring better,
OL,19,Fand whilst smaller than usual, there
OL,20,Fare still plenty to go around.
OL,23,APub: 05-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
